# UI design (project hook)

Follow the `ui-design` skill (personal: `~/.cursor/skills/ui-design`, or this repo’s copy).

1. Read **DESIGN.md** in this repo before creating or editing UI.
2. Reuse existing UI primitives. No second button/input/dialog.
3. Semantic tokens / CSS variables only. No raw hex. No default Tailwind palette as brand.
4. Spacing on the 4px scale. Surface density from DESIGN.md (`marketing` | `app` | `data` | `form` | `media`).
5. WCAG 2.2 AA: 4.5:1 text, 24px targets, visible focus, `prefers-reduced-motion`.
6. Empty, loading, error, disabled, permission states on every new screen.
7. After user-visible UI changes, verify in the browser at 375 / 768 / 1440 and fix what you see.
8. Forbidden: `transition-all`, `hover:scale-*` as a default, TypeUI / UIUX Pro Max catalogs.
9. Marketing/landing/storefront: honor `DESIGN.md` token freeze exactly. Diff CSS vs freeze before done. Paste the slop checklist in the reply. Do not retint hue to “fix” slop. Sibling palette overlap is allowed; whole-identity copycat without a written reason is not.
